Gregorian calendar for Persian, and fix two blind spots in translation

Calendar: fa-IR-u-ca-gregory — Gregorian dates with Persian text and
digits. The system stores and reasons in Gregorian throughout, so a
Jalali display meant converting between two calendars mentally.

Translation, found by actually running the app in English rather than
trusting the coverage check:

- Members and Clients rendered wholly in Persian in every language. Both
  pages were synchronous; layouts and pages render in parallel, so t()
  ran before the translator was primed and returned the source string.
  Every other page is fine only because it awaits data first.
- The extractor never saw table headers (header: '…') or add buttons
  (addLabel="…"). They arrive as props and never sit inside t(), so the
  check reported zero missing while they stayed Persian everywhere. Both
  forms are extracted now and translated at the point they render.
- Six strings had a translation that was never used because the literal
  and the key differed by a hamza or a zero-width space.

